PRETABLE.out -- i8259eoiirr (#574) -- the PRE-TABLE CHECK, written 2026-10-25 08:1x BEFORE any mutant table ran
(its mtime is the order proof).  Instrument: i8259_eoi_probe.py v2b, md5 2aa4570bd96f598a75d35987a3e8306e, 77 rows
(18 symptom rows), banked both-legs run pass2_20261025/fixlegs_080950/ (HEAD 77/77, FIX 77/77, CONTROL OK both).
Fix under test: design (G') in /tmp/gxt19/fix (binary e527ab18; dev_8259.c +78 -29, dev_gt.c +18 -1, devices.h +2).

1. SIBLING PARITY (each edited arm against its nearest sibling; an asymmetry is a row owed or a sentence owed)
   a. the specific-EOI arm (edited: ISR-only when in service, legacy consume otherwise) vs the non-specific arm
      (edited: lowest ISR bit).  Rows: `eoi acked`, `eoi acked3`, `eoi noack`, `masked eoi` (specific); `nonspec
      lowest`, `nonspec twice` (non-specific).  Asymmetry: the non-specific arm has NO legacy-consume branch (on HEAD
      its IRR effect was `irr &= ~isr` with isr always 0 -- a no-op), so an un-acknowledged 0x20 consumes nothing in
      either column.  SENTENCE OWED, recorded here: that is HEAD's behaviour kept, not a new refusal.
   b. the `case 0x0c` read arm (edited: acknowledges, one-shot) vs the `default` read arm (untouched, byte-identical:
      the raw scan).  Rows: `poll byte`, `poll isr`, `poll irr4`, `poll once`, `poll masked`, `quiet poll`.  The
      default arm has NO row: a read with current_command == 0 is OUTSIDE the contract (disclosed in the docstring).
   c. the two acknowledge sites: the poll read (pic1 rows `ack*`, pic2 rows `casc*`) vs the GT IACK read (`gt*`,
      `gtcasc*`).  Both rowed on both PICs.  Not rowed: a GT IACK read with NOTHING pending (returns last_int, as
      HEAD; OUTSIDE), a GT IACK WRITE (the read-only guard; no malta guest writes it; OUTSIDE), the MVME5500 path
      (pic1 == NULL; no witness machine; OUTSIDE).
   d. pic1 vs pic2: the poll, the EOI and the GT path are rowed on pic2 through the mc146818 line (`casc*`,
      `gtcasc*`); a MASKED poll on pic2 is not rowed (OUTSIDE; the mask logic is the same helper line).

2. CLAIM -> ROW (every added comment sentence asserting an observable consequence)
   "resets the highest-priority in-service bit (the lowest set ISR bit)"           -> `nonspec lowest`, `nonspec twice`
   "when the line is in service ... resets that ISR bit and leaves the request"   -> `eoi acked`, `eoi acked3`, `eoi acked isr`
   "when it is NOT ... the EOI still consumes the request as it always did"       -> `eoi noack`, `masked eoi`
   "the read after an OCW3 poll ... is the interrupt acknowledge"                  -> `poll isr`, `poll irr4`, `poll3 isr`
   "of the highest unmasked request -- the raw irr scan returned masked lines"     -> `poll masked`, `poll first`/`poll second`
   "One read per poll: later reads return the IRR"                                 -> `poll once`
   "Line 0 of pic1 is the 8253, whose pending-event count is retired here"         -> `rate storm` (band), `pit poll irr0`
   "a PCI interrupt-acknowledge READ is the acknowledge ... then in pic2"          -> `gt isr`, `gt irr4 after`, `gtcasc isr2`, `gtcasc isr8`
   "Nothing pending, no ISA PICs, or a write: last_int, as before"                 -> NO ROW (1c) -- sentence owed, recorded here
   "pic2's irq is the cascade line (bus_isa.c folds it into pic1 bit 2)"           -> `casc irr2`, `gtcasc irr2` (controls)

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD (per predicate the fix depends on; the partition the body induces; who writes each)
   specific-EOI hybrid predicate `d->isr & bit` -- body reads `d->irr`, `d->ier`, `d->irq`.  isr bit written by: the
   helper (set), both EOI arms (clear), DEVINIT (memset).  irr bit written by: bus_isa assert/deassert/fold, the
   helper (clear), the legacy branch (clear).  The four (isr bit, irr bit) cells for line 4: (1,0) after an ack with no
   re-assert -> `poll irr4`/`eoi acked isr`; (1,1) ack + re-assert -> `eoi acked`; (0,1) -> `eoi noack`; (0,0) ->
   `quiet *`.  Line 3: (1,1) `eoi acked3`, (1,0) `poll3 isr`.  Line 0: (1,0) `pit poll irr0`.  ier bit {0,1}: `masked
   eoi` (ier 1, isr 0) and `poll masked`.  EXHAUSTED for lines 4 and 3 on the body-tested cells; SAMPLED on line 0.
   helper `pending = irr & ~ier` {0, >0}: `quiet poll` (0) and every ack row (>0); `d == pic1 && n == 0 && ptr != NULL
   && *ptr > 0`: (pic1, n 0, >0) -> `rate storm`, `pit poll irr0`; (pic1, n != 0) -> `poll isr` etc.; (pic2) ->
   `casc isr8`, `gtcasc isr8`; (ptr NULL) UNREACHABLE on malta (DEVINIT(8253) always publishes) -- disclosed.
   `current_command` {0x0a, 0x0b, 0x0c, other}: 0x0c rowed everywhere; 0x0a/0x0b rowed as the readbacks; `other`
   (the default arm) OUTSIDE -- disclosed.
   G4 `writeflag == MEM_READ` {read, write}: write cell UNROWED (no malta guest writes the IACK register) -- disclosed;
   `n == 2 && pic2 != NULL` -> `gtcasc *`; `n2 >= 0` vs `n2 < 0`: n2 < 0 needs master bit 2 folded with no unmasked
   slave request -- the fold is recomputed on every ISA event, so the cell is UNREACHABLE short of a masking race;
   disclosed.

4. CHANNEL (per symptom row: the mutant it kills and the observable that differs under it)
   poll isr        M_noack_isr (helper does not set ISR)             ISR reads 0x00 instead of 0x10
   poll irr4       M_noack_irr (helper does not clear IRR)           IRR bit 4 reads 1 instead of 0
   poll once       M_sticky   (no revert to 0x0a after the ack)      second read 0x84/0x80 instead of the IRR
   eoi acked       B_eoi      (the EOI arm's IRR clear reinstated, unconditional)   IRR bit 4 reads 0 instead of 1
                   D_eoi_n4   (`(d->isr & bit) && (idata & 7) != 4`)                 same channel
                   D_eoi_ier  (`d->ier & bit` in place of `d->isr & bit`)            same channel (line 4 unmasked)
   eoi acked3      D_eoi_n3   (`... && (idata & 7) != 3`)            IRR bit 3 reads 0 instead of 1
   poll3 isr       M_noack_isr                                       ISR 0x00 instead of 0x08
   poll masked     D_scan_raw (`irr` in place of `irr & ~ier`)       0x84 instead of 0x00
   poll second     M_noack_irr                                       0x83 instead of 0x84
   isr both        M_noack_isr                                       0x00 instead of 0x18
   nonspec lowest  B_nonspec  (`isr = 0` reinstated)                 0x00 instead of 0x10
   casc isr2       M_noack_isr (pic1 path), B_poll                   0x00 instead of 0x04
   casc isr8       M_noack_isr (pic2 path)                           0x00 instead of 0x01
   pit poll irr0   M_noack_irr (line 0)                              1 instead of 0
   gt isr          B_gt       (the IACK read reverted to last_int)   0x00 instead of 0x10
   gt irr4 after   B_gt                                              1 instead of 0
   gtcasc isr2     B_gt, D_gt_nocasc (the `n == 2` branch dropped)   0x00 instead of 0x04 (isr8 likewise)
   rate storm      D_noretire (the decrement dropped), M_noack_irr   thousands of deliveries instead of 1..1000
   VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION check: every row above names a register or count that the named mutant changes; no row is
   a survive-only oracle.  Two mutant shapes have NO row and are recorded as EXPECTED ESCAPES, disclosed: D_gt_write
   (the read-only guard dropped: a WRITE to the IACK register would acknowledge; no row writes it) and D_fold (the
   manual cascade pre-fold re-added, the F2 defect: it strands a second slave request with the CPU line LOW -- a
   CPU-line observable with two slave sources pending, which no register row reads; OWED as a filed row, not built
   here, because the probe has no two-slave-source session).

5. THE PRESCRIBED TABLE (run from frozen copies in scratch clones under /tmp/gxt19/m_*, each with its own sentinel;
   the FIX column via GATE mode; score = rows green of 77; a mutant is KILLED when any row reds)
   (a)  L0: the base binary in GATE mode (the pre-fix build against the FIX column)     expected 59/77 (18 symptom reds)
   (c)  L3: /bin/false in GATE mode (the null medium)                                    expected CONTROL=FAIL, 0/77
   (b)  B_eoi: both EOI arms' IRR clears + recalcs reinstated verbatim (hybrid removed)   expected killed (eoi acked*)
        B_poll: the 0x0c read arm reinstated verbatim (raw scan, no ack, sticky)         expected killed (poll*, casc*)
        B_gt: the GT IACK case reinstated verbatim                                       expected killed (gt*, gtcasc*)
        B_nonspec: `isr = 0` reinstated in the 0x20 arm                                  expected killed (nonspec lowest)
   (d)  D_eoi_n4, D_eoi_n3, D_eoi_ier, D_scan_raw, D_noretire, M_sticky, D_gt_nocasc, M_noack_isr, M_noack_irr,
        D_gt_write (expected ESCAPE, disclosed), D_fold (expected ESCAPE on register rows, disclosed; owed CPU-line row)
   This list is DIFFED against any later row rewrite (the #490 lesson): a rewrite that drops a prescribed mutant or its
   row has dropped an obligation.

INSTRUMENT REVISION before table 1: v2c, md5 13490a35e2592dfb876189c4e55695aa (v2b plus a dead-medium fast path in run_session;
