CORRECTION, 2026-10-25 08:5x (before the table on the revised instrument; the pass-2 adjudicator GPT-6 Astra, DO NOT SHIP, Q2):
 * The CHANNEL line for `poll once` was WRONG.  As built in v2c (`build_ack`), the second read followed a second poll made with
   NOTHING pending, so a sticky poll of an empty IRR and the intended IRR read both return 0x00: M_sticky was predicted KILLED by a
   row that cannot see it.  v2d moves the one-shot row to the MASKED session -- the masked poll acknowledges nothing, the request
   stays pending, and the next command-port read returns the IRR 0x10 (one-shot) vs the poll byte 0x00 (sticky) vs 0x84 (HEAD).
   The v2c row is kept under the honest name `poll again` (it measures HEAD's unconsumed request, not the latch).
 * An UNPRESCRIBED (d) shape: dropping `if (n >= 0) odata = n;` in the GT read leaves `last_int` while both acknowledges run; the
   single-source rows `gt iack` (4) and `gtcasc iack` (8) stay green because last_int equals the acknowledged line there.  v2d adds
   the session `gtboth` (UART IRQ 4 and RTC IRQ 8 pending together): the acknowledge returns 8 (line 2 outranks line 4), HEAD's
   flat scan returns 4.  Prescribed mutant D_gt_noassign: `if (n >= 0) odata = n;` -> `;`.  Expected: killed by `gtboth iack`.
 * The table on v2c (SCORES.txt, first run) stands as the record of what it measured; the table of record is re-run on v2d, every
   mutant, from the frozen v2d copy.

