1. THE RETIRE GUARD (v2g block, lines "the retire guard (pic1 && n == 0 && ptr && *ptr > 0)"): the sentence "both observable only
   with a pending count >= 2, which only host time produces; filed pit8253retireguard with the band-row construction" is
   WITHDRAWN (F2d D1: Astra and GLM B; dev_8253.c:118-129 asserts line 0 on every tick while the count is positive, the only retire
   is pic8259_acknowledge's).  With ONE event in and line 0 masked, a foreign acknowledge (another master line by the poll; the
   slave's line through the GT cascade) followed by the LEGACY specific EOI of line 0 (not in service: HEAD's consume, no retire)
   and the next tick reads IRR bit 0 = 1 on the fix and 0 on D_retire_anyline / D_retire_anypic.  The two cells are therefore
   OWED REPAIR (clause (d) by its letter: body-tested conjuncts of a predicate the fix adds, reachable, measured escapes), NOT
   disclosed away.  The repair was attempted and classifier-stopped at 15:5x and, by the standing rule for a stopped attempt, is
   not retried in this round; it is carried by the row pit8253retireguard.  The cell (pic2, line != 0) was UNLISTED (F2d D2, GLM A)
   and is added here with the same disposition (no single-conjunct mutant fires only there; owed with the pair).
2. MAPPINGS (F2d D4, Astra): the non-specific arm with an EMPTY ISR is a no-op in both columns (HEAD's isr = 0 on an all-zero ISR;
   the fix's lowest-bit clear finds no bit) -- disclosed at 1.a above since 08:1x, now a cell of the v2g enumeration; "non-cascade
   acknowledge WITHOUT slave work" maps to the gt session's rows (line 4 acknowledged, slave ISR 0), gtmask being the case WITH
   slave work pending.
3. THE NON-SPECIFIC ARM'S "highest-instead: by construction (0x10 vs 0x08) -- not built": stands as a disclosure and is OWED as a
   mutant (D_nonspec_high; F2d D6), filed with pit8253retireguard.
